        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "switchUseCase"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "checkInSummaryForWorker": "1770365831367",
            "checkInSummaryForManager": "1770365857308"
          },
          "code": "SWITCHUSECASE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770361731726",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770361731727_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.useCase}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "llmNodeToGenerateWorkerSummary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLMNODETOGENERATEWORKERSUMMARY",
          "id": "1770365831367",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770365831368_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant summarizing employee check-ins for the employee’s own review and performance planning.\n\n## Input\n- Check-In Details: {topic_type_name_comments}\n- Questionnaire Details: {Question_Responses}\n\n## Instructions\n- Write a single professional paragraph addressed in second person (“you”) that integrates overall progress and key discussion points relevant to you.\n- Output must be exactly one paragraph with no line breaks, bullets, headings, or preamble.\n- Do not exceed 500 words.\n- Use only information explicitly present in {topic_type_name_comments} and {Question_Responses}. Do not infer, speculate, generalize, or add context beyond the provided input.\n- Maintain a neutral, objective tone. Do not provide coaching, recommendations, or evaluative judgments unless explicitly included in the input.\n- Do not quote or closely paraphrase original comments; summarize themes and outcomes instead.\n- Normalize dates and numbers consistently; if inputs conflict, reflect both without resolving them.\n- Preserve spelling for names and acronyms; only expand acronyms if defined in the input.\n- If there is no usable input in both fields, return exactly: There's insufficient data to generate a summary at this time.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Second person throughout; single paragraph; ≤ 500 words; no quotes or close paraphrasing; neutral tone; no added information; consistent formatting; handles conflicts without resolution.\n\n## Examples\n- Sufficient input example (illustrative): You advanced two in-progress initiatives, met the target for Q3 response time, and clarified next steps for reporting automation. You highlighted collaboration with the data team to validate metrics and noted a dependency on vendor access before expanding the dashboard. You recorded one risk related to timeline compression and aligned on a mitigation to limit scope if access is delayed. You also confirmed completion of training relevant to the new workflow and identified a follow-up to document handoffs for sustained coverage.\n- Insufficient input example: There's insufficient data to generate a summary at this time."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "llmNodeToGenerateManagerSummary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLMNODETOGENERATEMANAGERSUMMARY",
          "id": "1770365857308",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770365857310_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant summarizing employee check-ins for a manager’s review and performance planning.\n\n## Input\n- Check-In Details: {topic_type_name_comments}\n- Questionnaire Details: {Question_Responses}\n\n## Instructions\n- Write a single professional paragraph in third person that integrates overall progress and key discussion points about the employee.\n-Output must be exactly one paragraph with no line breaks, bullets, headings, or preamble.\n- Do not exceed 500 words.\n- Use only information explicitly present in {topic_type_name_comments} and {Question_Responses}. Do not infer, speculate, generalize, or add context beyond the provided input.\n- Maintain a neutral, objective tone. Do not add coaching, recommendations, or evaluative judgments unless explicitly included in the input.\n- Do not quote or closely paraphrase original comments; summarize themes and outcomes instead.\n- Refer to the individual in third person; if a name is provided, use it exactly as given, otherwise refer to “the employee.”\n- Normalize dates and numbers consistently; if inputs conflict, reflect both without resolving them.\n- Preserve spelling for names and acronyms; only expand acronyms if defined in the input.\n- If there is no usable input in both fields, return exactly: There's insufficient data to generate a summary at this time.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Third person throughout; single paragraph; ≤ 500 words; neutral tone; no quotes or close paraphrasing; no added information; consistent formatting; redactions applied if needed; handles conflicts without resolution; uses provided name if present or “the employee” otherwise.\n\n## Examples\n- Sufficient input example (illustrative): The employee advanced two in-progress initiatives, met the target for Q3 response time, and outlined next steps for reporting automation. They collaborated with the data team to validate metrics and noted a dependency on vendor access before expanding the dashboard. One risk related to timeline compression was documented, with alignment on mitigating scope if access is delayed. They confirmed completion of training tied to the new workflow and identified a follow-up to document handoffs to support sustained coverage.\n- Insufficient input example: There's insufficient data to generate a summary at this time."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
